  "id": "COMPOUND:12208 - PROTEIN:1692",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent pathway where the Influenza B virus B/Hong Kong/259/2010 hemagglutinin antigen, derived from MDCK cells and inactivated with propiolactone, acts as a target for magnesium levulinate, which in turn targets protein S100-A8. This relationship is supported by multiple independent paths, all of which indicate a direct interaction between the virus antigen and magnesium levulinate, followed by a shared target of protein S100-A8. The recurring involvement of magnesium levulinate as a mediator highlights a potential mechanism where the virus antigen may interact with this compound to modulate the expression or activity of S100-A8. The evidence suggests that the virus antigen may influence S100-A8 through a pathway involving magnesium levulinate, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
